WEBVTT

00:10:29.162 --> 00:10:30.412
On the plus side,

00:10:30.454 --> 00:10:34.912
we now have things like
Bayesian analysis of radiocarbon dates

00:10:34.954 --> 00:10:38.621
and theoretical approaches,
like the new materialisms.

00:10:39.496 --> 00:10:40.954
But in the process,

00:10:40.996 --> 00:10:44.287
archeology left the public behind.

00:10:44.329 --> 00:10:47.496
Shows like “What in the World?”
became less common

00:10:47.537 --> 00:10:50.787
and pseudoarcheology emerged
to fill the void.

00:10:52.954 --> 00:10:58.037
But we can all contribute
to changing how we think about the past.

00:10:58.079 --> 00:11:01.037
When you see a pseudoarcheological claim,